"selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5039e046-3a2d-50c1-a153-91577d91bce5" :question/math-academy-id "q-75732" :question/problem "![](images/31/312c7d003e2d856e55b3b5700402aa86b53e43dcd8f8650b4e04476b8be9b585.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $C$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-2.$ Find the vector $Cv.$" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cv & =-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](images/1e/1ef0448df9f0a37289e9792ce62e6c92203aeb4333f2b25f21c608b5253cf1fe.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49c501da-161c-53be-8349-571cc6a07975" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting the Product of a Matrix and an Eigenvector Given its Corresponding Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc9ed2b-5bc1-572f-8712-4696adf52dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5aeec63c36be20f6d54610d4ad90de8ea047db412fca7851d0267176783bdca3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393557} {:answer/id #uuid "b08019e9-4e7f-5cff-bd3e-a04f6a3d6b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3030aa3eb132ccd74991bff510393917e83a6683cce37d2c194c1526bef6e90.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393558} {:answer/id #uuid "75c07700-5db8-5e7b-8993-3c3e2f700a3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c272ff1454ac4ab9825e312f563c9bca08ac2800faa0e95ab45e8a5e827369da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393559} {:answer/id #uuid "55ce8068-c4b7-5b44-9053-a4d2e193284e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9e45156d033da0b7f5cb06d703e6bab2e65fae17f5ae7ae28374fab10f